{"code":"13-2071.00","title":"Credit Counselors","description":"Advise and educate individuals or organizations on acquiring and managing debt. May provide guidance in determining the best type of loan and explain loan requirements or restrictions. May help develop debt management plans or student financial aid packages. May advise on credit issues, or provide budget, mortgage, bankruptcy, or student financial aid counseling.","jobZone":4,"kinds":{"R":{"score":1,"share":0},"I":{"score":2.65,"share":0.1144},"A":{"score":1.8,"share":0.0555},"S":{"score":4.89,"share":0.2698},"E":{"score":4.73,"share":0.2587},"C":{"score":5.35,"share":0.3017}},"highPoints":["C","S","E"],"tasks":[{"id":18936,"text":"Create debt management plans, spending plans, or budgets to assist clients to meet financial goals.","core":true,"importance":4.9,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.76},{"id":18934,"text":"Assess clients' overall financial situations by reviewing income, assets, debts, expenses, credit reports, or other financial information.","core":true,"importance":4.86,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.81},{"id":18935,"text":"Calculate clients' available monthly income to meet debt obligations.","core":true,"importance":4.76,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.67},{"id":18933,"text":"Advise clients or respond to inquiries about financial matters in person or via phone, email, Web site, or Internet chat.","core":true,"importance":4.67,"relevance":90,"frequency":4.94},{"id":18945,"text":"Recommend strategies for clients to meet their financial goals, such as borrowing money through loans or loan programs, declaring bankruptcy, making budget adjustments, or enrolling in debt management plans.","core":true,"importance":4.67,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.76},{"id":18952,"text":"Explain general financial topics to clients, such as credit report ratings, bankruptcy laws, consumer protection laws, wage attachments, or collection actions.","core":true,"importance":4.65,"relevance":95.24,"frequency":4.75},{"id":1